## 8. How It Was Built — Development Approach

- **One platform at a time, proven real before moving on.** Rather than building all four adapters against a hope they'd work, YouTube was built first and pushed to a genuine successful publish before any further platform work started — de-risking the hardest, least certain part of the project early.
- **Local-first development.** Everything currently runs in Docker locally, matching the eventual AWS architecture closely enough that migrating to production is a deployment change, not a rewrite.
- **Defensive engineering learned from real debugging.** Several real issues were found and fixed during testing — silent failures were made loud and traceable, a database-wiping bug in a "reset" utility was caught and scoped safely, and account-selection UI was hardened to prevent accidentally publishing to the wrong (fake) account during a live demo. These weren't hypothetical risks — they were things that actually happened during development and were fixed before they could cause a real problem.

